# Everything below is a deliberate consequence of this package's coexistence
# design, not an oversight. See core/rpm/indi-stable-core.spec's header and
# DESIGN.md for the reasoning.
#
# There is one override file PER BINARY PACKAGE, and that is required rather
# than stylistic: dh_lintian installs a given file only into the package it is
# named for, and lintian rejects any line naming a different package as an
# "alien-tag". A single combined file therefore leaves the other packages'
# overrides silently INERT -- their tags stay hard errors -- which is exactly
# what the first Debian build produced.

# /opt is correct here: FHS 3.13 reserves it for add-on application software,
# and Debian Policy's prohibition binds packages shipped by Debian, which this
# third-party repository is not. It also keeps the install path identical
# across Fedora/RHEL/Debian/Ubuntu, so one documented path works everywhere.
indi-stable-core: dir-or-file-in-opt

# RPATH into the private libdir is the mechanism that stops these binaries
# resolving against -- or being resolved against -- a distribution INDI
# carrying the same SONAME. Removing it breaks the coexistence guarantee.
indi-stable-core: custom-library-search-path
